{"id":"mahabharata-6-105","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":105,"title":"पञ्चाधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 105 · Tenth day: the guards of Shikhandin","summary":{"en":"Dhritarashtra asks who protected Shikhandin in the Pandava army. Sanjaya describes how Bhishma, resolved to die, cuts down the Pandava ranks and stands like a mountain covered with clouds.","kn":"ಪಾಂಡವ ಸೈನ್ಯದಲ್ಲಿ ಶಿಖಂಡಿಯನ್ನು ಯಾರು ರಕ್ಷಿಸಿದರೆಂದು ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಸಾಯಲು ನಿಶ್ಚಯಿಸಿದ ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಪಾಂಡವ ಸಾಲುಗಳನ್ನು ಕಡಿದು ಮೋಡಗಳಿಂದ ಮುಚ್ಚಿದ ಪರ್ವತದಂತೆ ನಿಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"धृतराष्ट्र पूछते हैं कि पाण्डव सेना में शिखण्डी की रक्षा किसने की। संजय बताते हैं कि मरने का निश्चय किए भीष्म पाण्डव पंक्तियों को काटते हैं और बादलों से ढके पर्वत की तरह खड़े रहते हैं।","te":"పాండవసేనలో శిఖండిని ఎవరు కాపాడారని ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు అడుగుతాడు. చావుకు నిశ్చయించిన భీష్ముడు పాండవ వరుసలను నరికి మేఘాలు కమ్మిన పర్వతంలా నిలుస్తాడని సంజయుడు వర్ణిస్తాడు.","ta":"பாண்டவப் படையில் சிகண்டியைக் காத்தவர் யார் என்று த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் கேட்கிறான். சாவதில் உறுதியான பீஷ்மர் பாண்டவ அணிகளை வெட்டி மேகம் சூழ்ந்த மலை போல் நிற்பதைச் சஞ்சயன் கூறுகிறான்.","ml":"പാണ്ഡവ സേനയിൽ ശിഖണ്ഡിയെ ആരാണ് സംരക്ഷിച്ചതെന്ന് ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. മരിക്കാൻ ഉറച്ച ഭീഷ്മർ പാണ്ഡവ നിരകളെ വെട്ടിവീഴ്ത്തി മേഘങ്ങൾ മൂടിയ പർവതംപോലെ നിൽക്കുന്നതായി സഞ്ജയൻ വിവരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.105; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"कथं शिखण्डी गाङ्गेयमभ्यधावत्पितामहम् ।\nपाञ्चाल्यः समरे क्रुद्धो धर्मात्मानं यतव्रतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"How did the Panchala Shikhandin, angry in the battle, rush at the grandsire, the son of Ganga, righteous-souled and firm in his vows?"}},{"n":2,"text":"केऽरक्षन्पाण्डवानीके शिखण्डिनमुदायुधम् ।\nत्वरमाणास्त्वराकाले जिगीषन्तो महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who guarded Shikhandin, weapon raised, in the Pandava army, those great chariot-warriors hurrying at the hour for haste and eager to win?"}},{"n":3,"text":"कथं शांतनवो भीष्मः स तस्मिन्दशमेऽहनि ।\nअयुध्यत महावीर्यः पाण्डवैः सहसृञ्जयैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"How did mighty Bhishma son of Shantanu fight on that tenth day against the Pandavas and Srinjayas?"}},{"n":4,"text":"न मृष्यामि रणे भीष्मं प्रत्युद्यातं शिखण्डिनम् ।\nकच्चिन्न रथभङ्गोऽस्य धनुर्वाशीर्यतास्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I cannot bear that Shikhandin went against Bhishma in the battle. I hope his chariot was not broken, nor his bow shattered as he fought?"}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"नाशीर्यत धनुस्तस्य रथभङ्गो न चाप्यभूत् ।\nयुध्यमानस्य संग्रामे भीष्मस्य भरतर्षभ ।\nनिघ्नतः समरे शत्रूञ्शरैः संनतपर्वभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His bow did not shatter, nor was his chariot broken, as Bhishma fought in the battle, bull of the Bharatas, killing his enemies with bent-jointed arrows."}},{"n":6,"text":"अनेकशतसाहस्रास्तावकानां महारथाः ।\nरथदन्तिगणा राजन्हयाश्चैव सुसज्जिताः ।\nअभ्यवर्तन्त युद्धाय पुरस्कृत्य पितामहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Many hundreds of thousands of your great chariot-warriors, with hosts of chariots, elephants, and well-equipped horses, advanced to the battle, putting the grandsire in front."}},{"n":7,"text":"यथाप्रतिज्ञं कौरव्य स चापि समितिंजयः ।\nपार्थानामकरोद्भीष्मः सततं समितिक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Bhishma, victor in battles, as he had vowed, Kaurava, kept destroying the Parthas' army without pause."}},{"n":8,"text":"युध्यमानं महेष्वासं विनिघ्नन्तं पराञ्शरैः ।\nपाञ्चालाः पाण्डवैः सार्धं सर्व एवाभ्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that great archer fought, killing his foes with arrows, all the Panchalas together with the Pandavas tried to stop him."}},{"n":9,"text":"दशमेऽहनि संप्राप्ते तताप रिपुवाहिनीम् ।\nकीर्यमाणां शितैर्बाणैः शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the tenth day came, he scorched the enemy army, scattered by sharp arrows in hundreds and thousands."}},{"n":10,"text":"न हि भीष्मं महेष्वासं पाण्डवाः पाण्डुपूर्वज ।\nअशक्नुवन्रणे जेतुं पाशहस्तमिवान्तकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandavas, elder brother of Pandu, could not conquer the great archer Bhishma in the battle, who was like Death with noose in hand."}},{"n":11,"text":"अथोपायान्महाराज सव्यसाची परंतपः ।\nत्रासयन्रथिनः सर्वान्बीभत्सुरपराजितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, great king, Savyasachin, scorcher of foes, the unconquered Bibhatsu, by a stratagem frightened all the charioteers,"}},{"n":12,"text":"सिंहवद्विनदन्नुच्चैर्धनुर्ज्यां विक्षिपन्मुहुः ।\nशरौघान्विसृजन्पार्थो व्यचरत्कालवद्रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"roaring loudly like a lion, again and again twanging his bowstring, loosing floods of arrows, and moving about the battle like Time itself."}},{"n":13,"text":"तस्य शब्देन वित्रस्तास्तावका भरतर्षभ ।\nसिंहस्येव मृगा राजन्व्यद्रवन्त महाभयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Terrified by his sound, your men, bull of the Bharatas, fled in great fear, like deer from a lion."}},{"n":14,"text":"जयन्तं पाण्डवं दृष्ट्वा त्वत्सैन्यं चाभिपीडितम् ।\nदुर्योधनस्ततो भीष्ममब्रवीद्भृशपीडितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Pandava victorious and your army hard pressed, Duryodhana, deeply pained, spoke to Bhishma."}},{"n":15,"text":"एष पाण्डुसुतस्तात श्वेताश्वः कृष्णसारथिः ।\nदहते मामकान्सर्वान्कृष्णवर्त्मेव काननम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This son of Pandu, dear sir, with white horses and Krishna as charioteer, is burning up all my men, like fire in a forest."}},{"n":16,"text":"पश्य सैन्यानि गाङ्गेय द्रवमाणानि सर्वशः ।\nपाण्डवेन युधां श्रेष्ठ काल्यमानानि संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look, son of Ganga, at the armies fleeing everywhere, driven in the battle by the Pandava, best of fighters."}},{"n":17,"text":"यथा पशुगणान्पालः संकालयति कानने ।\nतथेदं मामकं सैन्यं काल्यते शत्रुतापन ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a herdsman drives a herd of cattle in a forest, so is this army of mine being driven, scorcher of foes."}},{"n":18,"text":"धनंजयशरैर्भग्नं द्रवमाणमितस्ततः ।\nभीमो ह्येष दुराधर्षो विद्रावयति मे बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Broken by Dhananjaya's arrows, it runs hither and thither; and here is Bhima, hard to withstand, routing my force."}},{"n":19,"text":"सात्यकिश्चेकितानश्च माद्रीपुत्रौ च पाण्डवौ ।\nअभिमन्युश्च विक्रान्तो वाहिनीं दहते मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki, Chekitana, the two Pandava sons of Madri, and valiant Abhimanyu are burning my army."}},{"n":20,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नस्तथा शूरो राक्षसश्च घटोत्कचः ।\nव्यद्रावयेतां सहसा सैन्यं मम महाबलौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"So too Dhrishtadyumna the hero and the rakshasa Ghatotkacha, both very strong, suddenly scattered my army."}},{"n":21,"text":"वध्यमानस्य सैन्यस्य सर्वैरेतैर्महाबलैः ।\nनान्यां गतिं प्रपश्यामि स्थाने युद्धे च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"As my army is struck down by all these mighty ones, Bharata, I see no other refuge, either to stand or to fight,"}},{"n":22,"text":"ऋते त्वां पुरुषव्याघ्र देवतुल्यपराक्रम ।\nपर्याप्तश्च भवान्क्षिप्रं पीडितानां गतिर्भव ॥","meaning":{"en":"except you, tiger among men, whose prowess is like a god's. You are able; quickly be the refuge of those in distress.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"एवमुक्तो महाराज पिता देवव्रतस्तव ।\nचिन्तयित्वा मुहूर्तं तु कृत्वा निश्चयमात्मनः ।\nतव संधारयन्पुत्रमब्रवीच्छंतनोः सुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, great king, your father Devavrata, son of Shantanu, thought for a moment, made up his mind, and, comforting your son, said:"}},{"n":24,"text":"दुर्योधन विजानीहि स्थिरो भव विशां पते ।\nपूर्वकालं तव मया प्रतिज्ञातं महाबल ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Duryodhana, understand this and be steady, lord of the people. I made a vow to you long ago, mighty one:"}},{"n":25,"text":"हत्वा दश सहस्राणि क्षत्रियाणां महात्मनाम् ।\nसंग्रामाद्व्यपयातव्यमेतत्कर्म ममाह्निकम् ।\nइति तत्कृतवांश्चाहं यथोक्तं भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Every day I shall kill ten thousand great-souled Kshatriyas and then leave the battle; that is my daily task.' And I have done just as I said, bull of the Bharatas."}},{"n":26,"text":"अद्य चापि महत्कर्म प्रकरिष्ये महाहवे ।\nअहं वा निहतः शेष्ये हनिष्ये वाद्य पाण्डवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today too I shall do a great deed in the great battle: either I shall lie slain, or I shall slay the Pandavas."}},{"n":27,"text":"अद्य ते पुरुषव्याघ्र प्रतिमोक्ष्ये ऋणं महत् ।\nभर्तृपिण्डकृतं राजन्निहतः पृतनामुखे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today, tiger among men, I shall repay my great debt, the debt of the food of my master, by being slain at the head of the army.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा भरतश्रेष्ठः क्षत्रियान्प्रतपञ्शरैः ।\nआससाद दुराधर्षः पाण्डवानामनीकिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, the best of the Bharatas, hard to assail, scorching the Kshatriyas with arrows, came up to the Pandava army."}},{"n":29,"text":"अनीकमध्ये तिष्ठन्तं गाङ्गेयं भरतर्षभ ।\nआशीविषमिव क्रुद्धं पाण्डवाः पर्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the son of Ganga stood in the middle of his army, bull of the Bharatas, like an angry venomous snake, the Pandavas surrounded him."}},{"n":30,"text":"दशमेऽहनि तस्मिंस्तु दर्शयञ्शक्तिमात्मनः ।\nराजञ्शतसहस्राणि सोऽवधीत्कुरुनन्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"On that tenth day, O king, showing his own power, that delight of the Kurus killed hundreds of thousands."}},{"n":31,"text":"पञ्चालानां च ये श्रेष्ठा राजपुत्रा महाबलाः ।\nतेषामादत्त तेजांसि जलं सूर्य इवांशुभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He took away the vigour of the best and mightiest Panchala princes as the sun with its rays takes up water."}},{"n":32,"text":"हत्वा दश सहस्राणि कुञ्जराणां तरस्विनाम् ।\nसारोहाणां महाराज हयानां चायुतं पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed ten thousand strong elephants with their riders, O great king, and ten thousand horses,"}},{"n":33,"text":"पूर्णे शतसहस्रे द्वे पदातीनां नरोत्तमः ।\nप्रजज्वाल रणे भीष्मो विधूम इव पावकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"and full two hundred thousand foot-soldiers, Bhishma, best of men, blazed in the battle like a smokeless fire."}},{"n":34,"text":"न चैनं पाण्डवेयानां केचिच्छेकुर्निरीक्षितुम् ।\nउत्तरं मार्गमास्थाय तपन्तमिव भास्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Not one of the Pandavas could look at him, like the sun scorching on its northward course."}},{"n":35,"text":"ते पाण्डवेयाः संरब्धा महेष्वासेन पीडिताः ।\nवधायाभ्यद्रवन्भीष्मं सृञ्जयाश्च महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those Pandavas, enraged and tormented by that great archer, and the Srinjaya great chariot-warriors, rushed at Bhishma to kill him."}},{"n":36,"text":"स युध्यमानो बहुभिर्भीष्मः शांतनवस्तदा ।\nअवकीर्णो महाबाहुः शैलो मेघैरिवासितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fighting many, Bhishma son of Shantanu, the mighty-armed, was covered like a mountain by dark clouds."}},{"n":37,"text":"पुत्रास्तु तव गाङ्गेयं समन्तात्पर्यवारयन् ।\nमहत्या सेनया सार्धं ततो युद्धमवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your sons surrounded the son of Ganga on every side with a great army, and the fighting went on."}}]}]}